WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.910
There sure are a lot of soldiers around...

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.790
They're nearly finished 
cleaning up after Ginnungagap.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.960
That means that the military now has

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.840
more men to spare to search 
for the Scrapped Princess.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.230
Sorry, we're not open yet.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.950
I'm looking for someone.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.770
A blonde-haired girl with blue eyes.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.730
Her name is Pacifica. Pacifica Cassul.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.740
"A Chanson for Fleeting Moments"

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.750
Done yet?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.890
Finished.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.590
How do I look?

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.050
Let me see, let me see!

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.690
Stop it.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.730
Stop it!

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.520
I said stop it!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.570
If I can't draw, I can't draw!

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:59.240
Then you should've said 
so in the first place!

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.490
I told you a dozen times!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:04.910
Oh, my.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:10.330
Let's go.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.790
Hey!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.720
What's with the little lady?

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.680
Maybe she doesn't like me anymore.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.380
I bet she's avoiding me.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.100
Subconsciously, anyway.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.140
You think it means she's got no 
memories of being on the run,

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.640
and she doesn't <i>want </i>to remember?

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.730
That's the feeling I get, anyway.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.230
It's complicated, huh?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.690
It sure is...

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.650
Even so, I think she's better off this way.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.850
Christopher, have you come to see me off?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.590
Baroness, I...

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:06.740
Chris, I'm fond of putting 
a happy face on things.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.940
Even if it's silly or naive,

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.640
I'm rather fond of such things.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.310
I'm fond of those people who are able

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.560
to earnestly speak of such 
things as freedom and equality.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.610
Because I don't have those things.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.860
I didn't want to sully the hands 
of such people with blood.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:30.120
So I made you and the others 
shoulder that burden.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.120
Baroness...

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.280
I won't make excuses.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.880
It's all right if you hate me.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.750
But if you should ever 
want to keep someone safe,

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.120
you must act as a shield for that person.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.560
Chris, you'll be fine.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.930
Have faith in yourself,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.520
and keep a firm grip on your own free will.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.040
I leave the rest up to you.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.810
Do I have something on my face?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.750
No, sir.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.360
I see.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.280
It's sudden, but I have orders for you.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.080
The Obstinate Arrows are hereby 
ordered to give top priority

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.120
to their mission of capturing 
the Scrapped Princess.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.940
Begin your search at once,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.790
and capture the Scrapped Princess.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.320
That's a bit unreasonable, don't you think?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.360
We don't even know if she's alive,

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.250
and we're to abandon all our other duties?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.130
Don't worry.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.780
These orders are only valid for three days.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:15.060
General Peters-Stahl has a high 
opinion of the Obstinate Arrows.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.020
He assigned a deadline of three days

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.230
after giving due consideration 
to the unit's abilities.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.380
What's that mean?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.230
In the event you are unable to capture 
the Scrapped Princess within three days,

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.820
the unit will be disbanded.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.750
I guess searching the city is useless...

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.190
My master.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.660
If you've shown up,

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.300
I guess that means <i>she </i>isn't around.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.640
I beg of you, at least get some sleep.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.010
You're ordering me to sleep?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.600
You've got some nerve.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.390
If your body were wounded, 
I would be able to heal it,

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.850
but I am unable to do anything 
about mental exhaustion.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.310
Do what you can.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.440
Hey!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.910
How long are you going to keep following me?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.200
I told you that I would 
stay and observe, didn't I?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.420
You're irritated, aren't you?

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.730
It's only natural when you've 
got a monster at your side.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.090
How much of the truth have 
you heard from Zefiris?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.660
The truth?

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.050
You mean how you betrayed humanity, 
became the invaders' pawns,

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.510
and finally became our guards to make sure

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.060
we'd stay penned up in 
our prison? <i>That </i>truth?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.140
I wouldn't have put it quite like that.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.520
Let me ask you this, then.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.020
What have those invaders done to you humans?

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.070
Pillaged you? Wiped you out?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.990
No, they haven't done either 
of those things to you.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.940
In which case, why do you think that 
they took the step of sealing you away?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.000
Has it ever felt to you people 
like you're locked away?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.500
It hasn't, has it?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.260
If you aren't aware that you're imprisoned,

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.220
it's no different from being free.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:10.510
You and your kind have killed lots of people.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.720
Because of your sister, 
the Providence Breaker.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.180
The system that locks this world away exists 
to protect humanity from extinction.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.850
The life form known as humanity 
is an irregular species

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:28.520
that possesses many inconsistencies 
in its behavioral norms.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:32.070
In the event that humanity were to make 
contact with another intelligent species,

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.770
there is a risk that these instabilities 
would result in damage to both parties.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:40.200
Humanity was preserved within this 
world's system before they went extinct

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.010
as a result of their ferocity.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.040
Humanity's level of civilization 
was also lowered

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:49.400
to prevent them from feeling any stress 
at realizing the size of their world.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:55.790
Doesn't having a stable environment 
make for excellent living conditions?

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.900
I suppose.

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:04.270
My kind can't overlook the existence of a 
being who may cause this world to crash.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:08.690
We have been given the task of 
protecting the humanity of this world.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:14.650
We aren't plotting to kill the Providence 
Breaker out of malice towards her.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.260
She is a curse left behind by Browning.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.660
A weapon meant to counteract our abilities.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.080
We are like oil and water.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.720
But it was not I who wished 
it to be that way,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.630
nor was it your sister.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.610
Shannon Cassul.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.130
You seem to want to simply 
classify us as evil,

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:38.340
but you ought to reconsider who it 
was that set this all in motion.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.700
If you must hate someone, hate the 
humans who lived 5,000 years ago.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.310
Awfully chatty today, aren't we?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.060
I suppose I am.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:51.020
Even when you're a monster, 
it isn't a pleasant feeling

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.280
to be the recipient of criticism 
when you've done nothing wrong.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.250
Any questions?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.630
After everyone has verified 
their individual search areas,

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.670
carry out your assignment immediately.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:18.680
Dismissed.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.240
All done.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.710
That's a pro for you! You're so fast!

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.990
How do I look? Let me see!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.120
Hey!

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.080
Wait for me, damn it!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.970
See you later.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.930
Break a horse's leg.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.130
Oh, shut up!

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.600
Quit your chattering and get lost!

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.060
As you wish...

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.940
Go off to work without a care in your heart!

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.270
Rest assured, I will look after 
things while you're away.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.440
In fact, don't bother ever 
coming back at all...

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.610
What's so funny?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.950
Nothing.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.530
In that case, I suppose I'll 
avail myself of your kind offer.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.370
Yes, just leave everything to me, Sir Leo.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.830
I will guard Miss Pacifica with my life if...

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.580
Wait just a minute, Mr. Skorpus!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.840
Please, haven't I said to call me Leo?

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:37.920
Then call <i>me </i>by the right 
name! It's "Pamela"!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.170
Of course, Miss Paci... I mean Pamela.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.880
That's better. Just so we're clear on that.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.590
Look after her, then.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.850
Sure.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.770
Ah, to be young...

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.320
A search for the Scrapped Princess?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.490
So you're saying that she is here in Sauer.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.700
No, sire. Just that there 
is a strong possibility.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.120
However, the military's top 
brass have been leaning

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.670
towards going to war ever 
since Ginnungagap was used.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:17.920
I've heard that they want 
to use her as a trump card.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.920
I'm so pathetic.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.630
If only I had more power...

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.890
Please don't blame yourself, sire.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.420
It's still not set in stone 
that we're going to go to war.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.290
It's proceeding smoothly.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.940
If we don't run into any problems,

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:44.240
we should be able to begin the 
fine-tuning work in a few days.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.400
But it's the fine-tuning 
that's the real issue, right?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.910
We can't even test-run them.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.170
If these don't work right,

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:50.990
they're gonna end up as nothing 
more than steel coffins.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:53.580
If we activate their main systems 
before they're fully outfitted,

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.270
they'll be sitting ducks for the Peacemakers.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:57.920
Even if that involves a 
certain amount of risk.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.420
I know, I know.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.960
That's why I'm grumbling.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.330
I understand your wanting to hurry,

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.300
but we barely survived that last attack.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.220
For now, let's make sure that 
everything is done right.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.220
I understand that, too.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.560
We wouldn't be standing here

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.940
in Giat right now if Natalie 
hadn't shown us the way here.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.690
Word has it that those three are still alive.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:21.270
I also need to see about paying those 
guys back for sinking the Skid.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:22.250
Right.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.900
Let's try to get these combat-ready 
as soon as possible.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.530
We don't have anywhere to call home now.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:32.870
I won't be able to die peacefully 
until we beat those Peacemakers.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.730
Welcome back.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.030
Yes, I've returned.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.860
Is something wrong?

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.870
No, it might just be my imagination,

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.540
but it seemed like there were even more 
soldiers in the streets than usual.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.500
You don't think they're...

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:19.000
I certainly hope I'm 
reading too much into it,

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.460
but it's possible that they're 
searching for Miss Pacifica.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.980
Yes, can I help you?

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.680
I heard that there's a girl

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.380
with blonde hair and blue eyes 
who works at this playhouse.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.930
There is, there is,

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.730
but I'd say that she's more 
of an old lady than a girl.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:41.650
Right?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.570
Yes, yes, it would be a bit of a stretch 
to call her a girl, wouldn't it?

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.680
The lady next door split this with me.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.330
She said she made too much.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:16.890
She must have it rough,

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.350
what with her husband drinking 
every day like that...

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.800
Pass me that.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:27.480
She says that their son used to be an 
Inquisitor for the Church of Mauser,

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:31.320
but he disappeared somewhere, saying, 
"I'm gonna do great things on my own!"

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:38.370
How is it?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.050
Is it good or is it bad?

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:42.370
What do you think?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.090
It's okay.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.350
You know, I think we've got a fly in here...

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.050
Want some tea?

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.010
What's with these?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.810
They were cheap.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.940
That's not what I meant.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:04.520
Get out! Fine! I will! Your cooking's lousy!

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:05.610
Get out! Get out!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.350
They're at it again.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.200
This is nice.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.360
Domestic disputes?

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.240
No, not that. Sitting here like this.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.390
What're you two doing here?

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.100
We have something important to tell you.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.060
The Scrapped Princess?

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.390
The Scrapped Princess...

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:49.560
What's that?

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:54.990
Put simply, she's someone that 
the whole world wants dead.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.780
The one in that revelation who's 
supposed to destroy the world?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:16:59.700
That's right.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.750
We were hoping that if she heard the 
words "Scrapped Princess," Paci...

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.490
Pamela's memories would come rushing back.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.040
It doesn't look like it worked.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.170
Did I do something bad?

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.800
I can't just take your word for that.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.130
Even so, it's the truth.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.220
I had hoped that I wouldn't 
have to bring this up,

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.550
but it looks like I'll have to tell you.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.350
What're you talking about?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:23.020
Some soldiers came to the playhouse 
earlier, asking questions.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.180
Questions?

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.770
I don't think we have much time.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.810
And that's why we've come to 
take Miss Pamela away with us.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:33.780
Hey, stop talking about me like 
I'm not sitting right here!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.210
Please understand.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.450
We can't waste any more time!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.740
Soldiers might show up here 
while we're talking like this.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.750
Wait a minute, you show up out 
of the blue and expect me to...

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:45.330
Go where?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.540
You say you're going to take her with 
you, but where do you plan to take her?

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:53.300
Um... Well, as to where, 
we're not exactly sure.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.050
Unbelievable.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.630
You've only thought about running away?

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.260
You haven't considered where 
you're going to run <i>to</i>?

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:07.190
I can't just hand over Pamela to a couple of 
half-baked kids with a "Fine, off you go."

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.230
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:12.940
Do you seriously think you can make it 
out of the city with just that one sword?

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:16.190
On my honor as a knight, I'll 
see Miss Pamela out safely.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.740
Talk about naive.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.990
Those soldiers aren't so soft that you 
can fight through them with spirit alone.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.160
Are you saying that <i>you 
</i>can protect her, then?

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.120
At the very least, I'd be more 
useful to her than you would.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.800
Want to put that to the test?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.310
Hey, wait a minute, you two!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.930
Cut it out!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:53.780
Don't!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.610
Who is it?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.570
It's me. It's Sley.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.490
It's somebody I know.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.180
I sure have a lot of visitors today...

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.490
What do you want?

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.200
Have a minute?

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.160
I have company.

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:10.680
Let's talk outside.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.170
Sure.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.930
It's been a long time, Wraith.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.330
Don't call me by my old code name, not now.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:19.630
I'm not a Blackhawk anymore.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.340
Your resignation was never accepted.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:25.050
You're currently considered a reservist.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:27.350
Like I care. Anyway, what do you want?

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:28.920
Slow, aren't you?

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:30.810
I've come for you. To take you back.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.270
As you know, we're going to 
be marching on Giat soon.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:37.480
There'll be plenty of sabotage and 
assassinations in the near future.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.320
We'll have a lot more work to do.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.820
So?

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:44.280
We can't afford to let valuable 
talent like you loaf around anymore.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.660
It's only natural for me to come here, right?

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:47.950
Like I said,

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.810
I don't have any intention of 
going back to the military.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:50.790
Leave me alone.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.200
I think that's a real shame.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.410
But I don't. Go away.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.550
That look says that nothing I 
can say will change your mind.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.810
What do you think you're doing?!

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:10.100
You know you can't live a normal life, 
not with all that blood on your hands!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.180
Can't I?

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:13.350
Stop living in a dream world.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:14.310
Am I?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.280
Have a good life.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.470
Unexpected situation, classification 7.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.520
Pacifica Cassul located at Wraith's hideout.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.660
Request troop mobilization for 
confirmation and capture. Message ends.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.430 --> 00:22:39.460
Royal Forces soldiers descend on Furet's 
lodgings to capture the Scrapped Princess.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:41.380
Pacifica and the others manage to escape,

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:43.500
but what will happen to her now?

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:46.460
Will her happy, carefree days come to an end?

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.050
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:49.300
"Back Alley Elegy."

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
